# AutoFish — .NET Conventions

## Project Structure
- **`src/AutoFish.Contracts/`** — Active. C# models + serialization for bridge contracts. Target `net10.0`, implicit usings, nullable enabled.
- **`src/AutoFish.App/`** — **Frozen legacy.** WinForms GUI kept for reference. Do not add new live-window automation here.

## Code Style
- **Positional records** for contract models (e.g., `public sealed record FishingProfile(...)`).
- **`IReadOnlyList<T>`** for array properties — immutable by contract.
- **Nullable reference types** enabled project-wide (`<Nullable>enable</Nullable>`).
- **System.Text.Json** for all serialization. Use `ContractJson.Options` as the single source of truth.
- **Snake_case_lower** enum serialization (`JsonStringEnumConverter` with `SnakeCaseLower`).

## Validation
```powershell
dotnet build AutoFish.sln --configuration Release
```
Run `.\scripts\run-local-checks.ps1` to validate contracts + profiles + Python + Lua together.

## What NOT To Do
- Do not add new live-window automation to `AutoFish.App`.
- Do not add Newtonsoft.Json — the project uses System.Text.Json exclusively.
- Do not add mutable properties to contract models — records are sealed and immutable.
- Do not change `CurrentContractVersion` without updating schemas and Lua constants.
